    <VI_Package_Configuration_File>Toast Notifications for LabVIEW.vipc</VI_Package_Configuration_File>
    <Description>
      <One_Line_Description_Summary>Display interactive Windows toast notifications from LabVIEW and receive button actions and text replies.</One_Line_Description_Summary>
      <Description>Toast Notifications for LabVIEW lets you show native Windows notifications from your LabVIEW application. Use it to notify an operator when a long test finishes, open a report from a notification button, or ask for a short reply.

Compose a toast with ToastBuilder or display one from an XML string. The included activation handler delivers button arguments and submitted text as LabVIEW User Events. You can also implement your own handler to route activations into your application.

The package includes a LabVIEW project with four examples covering text replies, multiple actions, link buttons, and XML notifications.</Description>
      <Copyright/>
      <Packager>Loïc Wohleber</Packager>
      <URL>https://github.com/loicwoh/ToastNotifications</URL>
      <Release_Notes>1.0.0:
- Features:
  - Compose Windows toast notifications with text, buttons, and text input.
  - Receive activation arguments and submitted text in LabVIEW.
  - Open a web link from a notification button.
  - Export a composed toast as XML and display a toast from an XML string.
  - Receive activations through the included User Event handler or implement a custom handler.
- Examples:
  - Run four examples from the dedicated LabVIEW examples project.</Release_Notes>
    </Description>
